857c808a43f87f0c1f78ec171f23946288","event_uuid":"27c56913-0ec9-498f-977f-e58e45e9f8a6","position":{"commit_sha":"1588884e502432030c1dc1fde8f4c0c43d67f72e","position":"1786497502241433001-27c56913-0ec9-498f-977f-e58e45e9f8a6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c805541de15fbb9a4340e5793875b168613f571e212567a81276baaabbaa5a0b","event_uuid":"df30fcaf-959d-48c5-b30d-70b93b7db614","position":{"commit_sha":"ce419b663b61d25669c4958a1354f84227408819","position":"1786499252388989472-df30fcaf-959d-48c5-b30d-70b93b7db614"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"22250fe97d3ae795ca73229a23eee9f351d60c9c19f6d20cb5b03784d4b32b36","event_uuid":"107dc236-766a-41c6-b427-a6496edfb9f5","position":{"commit_sha":"ebc8666026e5445c9a4076171c77c2a7a0fe31e3","position":"1786500908405584001-107dc236-766a-41c6-b427-a6496edfb9f5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f8e31f8bd1c9e135135b4fcc5332582095dabfaf0db4f9632bfb3ec30e36505a","event_uuid":"0bb51184-7494-4373-ae04-e621e76b40d2","position":{"commit_sha":"21cc039b7a603036a868325e365adf8891533108","position":"1786500916121902001-0bb51184-7494-4373-ae04-e621e76b40d2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation landed for review as Gerrit change 1602 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1602).\n\nPatch set 1 passed LLM-Review +1 but took Verified -1 from tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py: that guard sources every MCP tool mechanically from list_tools() and fails any new one not classified as CANONICAL / EXEMPT_GENERIC / NO_SCHEMA_EXEMPT. It lives under tests/interfaces/, so the plan's AC6 verify command (pytest tests/unit -k mcp) could not have caught it.\n\nResolution, and a correction to the plan: the plan argued that src/rebar/schemas/ was NOT needed because check_mcp_models.MODEL_SCHEMAS is opt-in. That was wrong — the coverage guard's classification is not opt-in. Since the tool returns a genuinely structured {ok, verdict, reason, verified_at_sha, signed_at} shape rather than a string ack, the honest classification is CANONICAL, which requires a real canonical schema. Added src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json plus the PLAN_REVIEW_STATUS constant and OUTPUT_SCHEMAS entry (the every-schema-file-is-wired guard requires wiring), keyed by MCP tool name like grounding_info because the CLI reaches this read through 'review-plan --status' rather than its own subcommand. The ticket's original Scope line naming src/rebar/schemas/ was therefore right; file_impact now records all eight paths.\n\nSecond deviation: adding a nested tool pushed register_read_tools past its FROZEN McCabe ceiling (31 -> 32) in the shrink-only complexity baseline. Rather than raise a locked baseline, the tool is registered from a small module-level _register_plan_review_tools, following the seam register_bridge_tools already established in the same file.\n\nLocal gates green: ruff, mypy, MCP model schema drift, gen_mcp_reference.py --check, tests/unit -k mcp (48 passed), and the full tests/interfaces suite (1760 passed, 12 skipped) including live validation of the tool's real output against the new schema.","timestamp":1786500916121902001}],"created_at":1785949495508791001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"dcd872f4-b18d-4b73-8adb-791870dcc193","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"94a3-1323-3497-4f59"},{"link_uuid":"df30fcaf-959d-48c5-b30d-70b93b7db614","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"37eb-7ced-0563-47e7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe plan-review attestation currency check `rebar review-plan <id> --status` is a read-only,\nno-LLM, no-network query that answers \"should I re-gate before I implement?\". It is exported\nfrom the library (`rebar.llm.plan_review_status`) and exposed on the CLI, but there is NO MCP\ntool for it. An MCP-only agent can therefore never ASK whether its attestation is current — it\nonly discovers staleness by attempting a `claim` or a `transition ... closed` and reading the\nresulting error.\n\nFound while sweeping every attestation refusal surface for bug 94a3-1323-3497-4f59, which made\nthe refusal messages name what changed. That sweep helps a CLI agent immediately; an MCP agent\nstill has to provoke a refusal to learn anything, which is the parity gap.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a read-only MCP tool `plan_review_status` alongside the existing read tools in\n`src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py`, registered by `register_read_tools` with the `READ_ONLY`\nannotation preset (so it is present under `REBAR_MCP_READONLY` and absent from the write\nregistrar). Its body is a thin delegation to `rebar.llm.plan_review_status(ticket_id)` —\nthe SAME function the CLI's `--status` branch calls — imported lazily inside the tool body\nso the `[agents]`-extra import cost is not paid at read-registrar import time and so the\ndelegation is observable (patching `rebar.llm.plan_review_status` changes the tool's answer).\n\nIts return annotation is a new `PlanReviewStatusOut` pydantic model in\n`src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` (where every other MCP output model lives — the ticket's original\nscope guessed `src/rebar/schemas/`, but the JSON-Schema files there are only needed for the\nsubset of models listed in `check_mcp_models.MODEL_SCHEMAS`, which this additive model does\nnot join). The model declares the documented\n`{ok, verdict, reason, verified_at_sha, signed_at}` shape and inherits the permissive\n`extra=\"allow\"` base, following `VerifySignatureResultOut`.\n\n`docs/mcp-reference.md` is GENERATED by `scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py` from the server's own\nregistrars and is guarded by a CI drift gate, so the doc row is produced by regenerating the\nfile, not by hand-editing it.\n\nWhy this rather than widening an existing tool: `show_ticket` already carries a derived\n`plan_review_health` payload, but that is relationship/phase health, not the claim-gate\ncurrency verdict — overloading it would conflate two different questions and change an\nexisting tool's contract. A dedicated read-only tool is additive and matches how the CLI\nalready separates the two.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py` — the new read-only `plan_review_status` tool.\n- `src/rebar/_mcp_models.py` — the `PlanReviewStatusOut` output model.\n- `docs/mcp-reference.md` — regenerated so the read-tool inventory lists the tool.\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py` — the new tests.\n\nBehaviour-preserving for every existing surface: no existing tool, model, CLI verb, or\nlibrary function is modified; this change is purely additive.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: a ticket with a current attestation returns `ok: true`, `verdict: \"certified\"`.\n- Failure path: a ticket with no attestation returns `ok: false`, `verdict: \"unsigned\"`.\n- Delegation: patching `rebar.llm.plan_review_status` changes the tool's output.\n- The tool is registered in the MCP read-tool set and is absent from the write set (it must\n  not be gated by readonly mode).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — A read-only MCP tool named `plan_review_status` is registered by\n      `register_read_tools` and is NOT registered by `register_write_tools`.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k inventory`\n- [ ] AC2 — For a ticket whose plan-review attestation is current the tool returns\n      `ok: true` and `verdict: \"certified\"`.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k certified`\n- [ ] AC3 — For a ticket with no plan-review attestation the tool returns `ok: false` and\n      `verdict: \"unsigned\"`.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k unsigned`\n- [ ] AC4 — The tool delegates to `rebar.llm.plan_review_status` rather than reimplementing\n      the check; patching that function changes the tool's output.\n      Verify: `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k delegat`\n- [ ] AC5 — `docs/mcp-reference.md` lists `plan_review_status` in its Read-only section and\n      is not stale with respect to its generator.\n      Verify: `grep -q '`plan_review_status`' docs/mcp-reference.md && python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check`\n- [ ] AC6 — No existing behaviour regresses: lint, typecheck, and the MCP + doc-generator\n      unit tests pass.\n      Verify: `make lint && make typecheck && python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k \"mcp\"`","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_reads.py","reason":"register the read-only plan_review_status MCP tool via a module-level _register_plan_review_tools"},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_models.py","reason":"add the PlanReviewStatusOut output model backing the tool outputSchema"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_status.schema.json","reason":"canonical JSON Schema for the tool result, required to classify it CANONICAL in the MCP output-schema coverage guard"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":"PLAN_REVIEW_STATUS constant and OUTPUT_SCHEMAS entry (every-schema-file-is-wired guard)"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/check_mcp_models.py","reason":"map PlanReviewStatusOut to its schema for the MCP model drift gate"},{"path":"docs/mcp-reference.md","reason":"regenerated read-tool inventory listing plan_review_status"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py","reason":"unit tests for inventory, certified, unsigned, and delegation"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_output_schema_coverage.py","reason":"classify the tool CANONICAL and drive it on the seeded store"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","37eb-7ced-0563-47e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ec547224-2213-4fbb-8743-da949aef140f","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"86c8-4b91-5257-4cca","ticket_type":"task","title":"No MCP tool for `review-plan --status`: MCP agents cannot ask if an attestation is current","verify_commands":[{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k inventory","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"read-only MCP tool plan_review_status registered by register_read_tools and absent from write tools"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k certified","dd_id":"AC2","dd_text":"current attestation returns ok true and verdict certified"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k unsigned","dd_id":"AC3","dd_text":"no attestation returns ok false and verdict unsigned"},{"command":"python -m pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py -q -k delegat","dd_id":"AC4","dd_text":"tool delegates to rebar.llm.plan_review_status"},{"command":"grep -q plan_review_status docs/mcp-reference.md && python scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py --check","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"docs/mcp-reference.md lists the tool and is not stale"},{"command":"make lint && make typecheck && python -m pytest tests/unit -q -k mcp","dd_id":"AC6","dd_text":"no regression: lint, typecheck, mcp unit tests"}]},"source_event_uuids":["bdb1967e-f32b-4fbb-b3ee-0c6359d4d8de","dcd872f4-b18d-4b73-8adb-791870dcc193","fbe8ee2b-ba3f-4bd6-a66d-eb655efa90d7","c8cd620f-2013-447b-8a5f-7698f5d5d583","4fe98e72-9909-4bb8-9e45-1c884e10df43","6c992ef5-0025-44bf-9f9e-88c11919de2c","ec547224-2213-4fbb-8743-da949aef140f","27c56913-0ec9-498f-977f-e58e45e9f8a6","df30fcaf-959d-48c5-b30d-70b93b7db614","107dc236-766a-41c6-b427-a6496edfb9f5","0bb51184-7494-4373-ae04-e621e76b40d2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786500916121902002,"uuid":"8704a8e0-6a84-4e13-a84e-a8088798794d"}